WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.896
[MUSIC PLAYING]

00:00:05.388 --> 00:00:06.930
SPEAKER: Give me
one minute, and I'll

00:00:06.930 --> 00:00:09.600
show you how Google Kubernetes
Engine can help you modernize

00:00:09.600 --> 00:00:12.170
your existing application.

00:00:12.170 --> 00:00:14.160
GKE is an
enterprise-grade platform

00:00:14.160 --> 00:00:16.890
for stateful and stateless
containerized apps.

00:00:16.890 --> 00:00:18.630
It offers managed
Kubernetes and is

00:00:18.630 --> 00:00:22.020
comprised of a high-availability
control plane that Google

00:00:22.020 --> 00:00:25.290
manages and operates,
nodes, which hold the pods,

00:00:25.290 --> 00:00:28.250
and your connected
Google Cloud Services.

00:00:28.250 --> 00:00:33.140
You can interact with it using
kubectl or the cloud console.

00:00:33.140 --> 00:00:34.985
GKE increases
developer productivity

00:00:34.985 --> 00:00:36.860
with pre-built deployment
templates featuring

00:00:36.860 --> 00:00:39.710
portability and integrated tools
to accelerate app development

00:00:39.710 --> 00:00:41.120
and deployment cycles.

00:00:41.120 --> 00:00:42.620
It simplifies
platform operations

00:00:42.620 --> 00:00:45.810
with auto-scale, auto-upgrade,
and auto-repair features.

00:00:45.810 --> 00:00:47.390
It is secure by
default, including

00:00:47.390 --> 00:00:48.860
data encryption
and vulnerability

00:00:48.860 --> 00:00:50.760
scanning of container images.

00:00:50.760 --> 00:00:52.910
And it supports integrated
cloud monitoring

00:00:52.910 --> 00:00:54.380
with infrastructure,
application,

00:00:54.380 --> 00:00:56.480
and Kubernetes-specific views.

00:00:56.480 --> 00:00:58.640
GKE can help modernize
your applications,

00:00:58.640 --> 00:01:00.380
create a continuous
delivery pipeline,

00:01:00.380 --> 00:01:02.357
or migrate your
existing tutor app.

00:01:02.357 --> 00:01:04.940
Next time you're thinking about
modernizing your apps quickly,

00:01:04.940 --> 00:01:07.508
take a minute to look at
Google Kubernetes Engine.

00:01:07.508 --> 00:01:09.675
For more info, check out
cloud.google.com/kubernetes

00:01:09.675 --> 00:01:12.060
engine.

